  "courseSlug": "the-complete-guide-to-angular-2",
  "courseTitle": "Angular - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "6656286",
      "title": "Understanding Navigation Paths",
      "lectureOrder": 453,
      "videoOrder": 415,
      "sourceHash": "ec97ae6b8e1a3ef42df716f0fee71a34f06ec66735bd671941109abe0600aa80",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.31,
          "end": 3.9,
          "en": "Lecturer: In the last lecture, we added",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.9,
          "end": 7.02,
          "en": "this navigation and I also mentioned that you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.02,
          "end": 10.56,
          "en": "can change the way you use your paths here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.56,
          "end": 13.14,
          "en": "Right now we use slash slash servers,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.14,
          "end": 15.66,
          "en": "or even with this more complex notation,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.66,
          "end": 18.75,
          "en": "we have slash users as the first element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.75,
          "end": 21.51,
          "en": "Now, what happens if we just use servers here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 21.51,
          "end": 24.87,
          "en": "like this and just use users like this?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 24.87,
          "end": 27.84,
          "en": "Let's save this without the leading slash.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 27.84,
          "end": 31.02,
          "en": "Now if we click there on our links",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 31.02,
          "end": 36.02,
          "en": "you'd still see this works absolutely fine. Nothing changed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 36.54,
          "end": 41.54,
          "en": "Now let's go to our servers component template file here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 41.64,
          "end": 45.72,
          "en": "and for now let's quickly add a anchor tele-element here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 45.72,
          "end": 50.72,
          "en": "where we also add a router link where I add servers again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 51.24,
          "end": 54.03,
          "en": "Reload page would be a fitting description.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 54.03,
          "end": 56.82,
          "en": "So on this service component, I now edit this router link",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 56.82,
          "end": 58.59,
          "en": "where I basically want to make sure that I",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 58.59,
          "end": 61.5,
          "en": "stay on the service page, which I'm already on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 61.5,
          "end": 64.56,
          "en": "So if you go to service here, we see the reload page here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 64.56,
          "end": 68.4,
          "en": "and if I click it, you'll see we got an error.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 68.4,
          "end": 71.64,
          "en": "This error here occurs because it doesn't find a route",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 71.64,
          "end": 74.73,
          "en": "which is servers slash servers.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 74.73,
          "end": 78.48,
          "en": "Now this error won't occur if, on the service component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 78.48,
          "end": 82.05,
          "en": "I turned this to slash service, so to an absolute path.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 82.05,
          "end": 84.6,
          "en": "It was a relative path.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 84.6,
          "end": 88.26,
          "en": "Here, if we now have our console still open,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 88.26,
          "end": 91.26,
          "en": "and I click reload page, nothing occurs here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 91.26,
          "end": 94.86,
          "en": "Nothing or error occurs because now it simply navigates",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 94.86,
          "end": 99.36,
          "en": "to local host 4,200 slash servers as you can see down there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 99.36,
          "end": 102.69,
          "en": "And if we turn this back to a relative path",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 102.69,
          "end": 105.21000000000001,
          "en": "the difference was that now",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 105.21000000000001,
          "end": 108.18,
          "en": "it tries to go slash service service.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 108.18,
          "end": 111.15,
          "en": "So with a relative path it always appends",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 111.15,
          "end": 114.33,
          "en": "the path you specify in the router link to the end",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 114.33,
          "end": 115.74000000000001,
          "en": "of your current path.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 115.74000000000001,
          "end": 118.22999999999999,
          "en": "And important here, the current path depends",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 118.22999999999999,
          "end": 120.33,
          "en": "on which component you're currently on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 120.33,
          "end": 124.35,
          "en": "That is why we could remove that in our navigation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 124.35,
          "end": 127.41,
          "en": "where we always use relative paths because that isn't",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 127.41,
          "end": 128.85,
          "en": "our root component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 128.85,
          "end": 131.46,
          "en": "This component is not loaded through the router,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 131.46,
          "end": 135.45,
          "en": "so this root component always sits at local host",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 135.45,
          "end": 137.88,
          "en": "4,200 slash nothing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 137.88,
          "end": 140.85,
          "en": "So this is always at our root level, which is why",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 140.85,
          "end": 144.03,
          "en": "we can use relative paths here, too.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 144.03,
          "end": 147.12,
          "en": "But one layer below that, once we loaded a route,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 147.12,
          "end": 150.45,
          "en": "for example, the service component, this page is only loaded",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 150.45,
          "end": 152.57999999999998,
          "en": "if we are at slash servers,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 152.57999999999998,
          "end": 156,
          "en": "So if we add a relative route here, this will now",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 156,
          "end": 158.22,
          "en": "get appended to this route we are on,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 158.22,
          "end": 162.32999999999998,
          "en": "So it will try to load servers slash servers, and therefore",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 162.32999999999998,
          "end": 165.39,
          "en": "it gives us an error in our case because we haven't",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 165.39,
          "end": 169.26,
          "en": "registered a servers slash servers route.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 169.26,
          "end": 172.68,
          "en": "Now, of course, using relative paths inside",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 172.68,
          "end": 175.62,
          "en": "of active components, active routes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 175.62,
          "end": 178.74,
          "en": "might be a nice thing if you have nested routes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 178.74,
          "end": 181.62,
          "en": "Right now it'll only break the app though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 181.62,
          "end": 183.78,
          "en": "Now you can also use relative paths",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 183.78,
          "end": 185.46,
          "en": "with dot slash at the beginning.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 185.46,
          "end": 188.1,
          "en": "This is the same as having nothing there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 188.1,
          "end": 192.87,
          "en": "And you can even navigate around like in a folder directory.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 192.87,
          "end": 197.67000000000002,
          "en": "You could add dot dot slash which means go up one level,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 197.67000000000002,
          "end": 202.05,
          "en": "and then add this to the path here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 202.05,
          "end": 205.26,
          "en": "Now, if we do this inside of our servers component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 205.26,
          "end": 207.42000000000002,
          "en": "you will see, if I hover over this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 207.42000000000002,
          "end": 211.26,
          "en": "now it, again, only tries to load slash servers",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 211.26,
          "end": 213.36,
          "en": "and therefore we don't see an error",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 213.36,
          "end": 216.27,
          "en": "because now it first goes back one level",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 216.27,
          "end": 219.12,
          "en": "which basically is to just our root path.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 219.12,
          "end": 220.98,
          "en": "So it removes one path,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 220.98,
          "end": 223.92000000000002,
          "en": "and important path depends on the route you're on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 223.92000000000002,
          "end": 227.73,
          "en": "So if you were on servers slash something,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 227.73,
          "end": 231.27,
          "en": "and this would load this component, it would remove both.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 231.27,
          "end": 235.35,
          "en": "So this does not necessarily only remove one segment here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 235.35,
          "end": 238.59,
          "en": "it removes the currently loaded segment, you could say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 238.59,
          "end": 240.24,
          "en": "So in this case it removes this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 240.24,
          "end": 244.26,
          "en": "And then adds slash servers again, which is why this works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 244.26,
          "end": 246.42,
          "en": "And this is how you can navigate around",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 246.42,
          "end": 249.15,
          "en": "absolute paths with a slash at the beginning",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 249.15,
          "end": 252.63,
          "en": "which will always get appended to the root domain,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 252.63,
          "end": 256.44,
          "en": "relative paths without a slash or with dot slash",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 256.44,
          "end": 259.71,
          "en": "which means added to the currently loaded path,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 259.71,
          "end": 263.37,
          "en": "or dot dot slash, and you can even add more of them,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 263.37,
          "end": 268.2,
          "en": "to say well go back once path, go back another path,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 268.2,
          "end": 272.25,
          "en": "So always seen from the currently loaded component on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 272.25,
          "end": 275.55,
          "en": "And if that is something which is not 100% clear,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 275.55,
          "end": 277.26,
          "en": "you will see throughout this module,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 277.26,
          "end": 279.57,
          "en": "But also feel free to play around with it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 279.57,
          "end": 282,
          "en": "Add your own routes, add some nesting,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 282,
          "end": 285.57,
          "en": "add more complex paths, and see how this works out.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 285.57,
          "end": 288.06,
          "en": "But for now, let's continue with our application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 288.06,
          "end": 290.4,
          "en": "I will remove this reload page link,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 290.4,
          "end": 292.1,
          "en": "and let's enhance this a bit more.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
